19-06-14T11:06:11-07:00","id":1318506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1203449-request-editable-pdf-character-sheet?p=1318465#post1318465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there's some kind of eldritch chicanery at work here, Mr G. When the magic word 'sheets' is uttered aloud there's a clap of thunder, a little ozone frisson, and there you are, tipping your fedora with a knowing smile as you hand out PDF miracles.<br /> <br /> My next character is gonna be a scion of you. Sure, he may not punch too many Jotnar to death with his fists but he'll damn well make them feel inadequate when he breaks out their character sheets and shows them how awful their stats are.</div> </div> </div> </div>He has a special knack, he can spend a legend to materialise a high quality interactive sheet for any game, even those yet to be launched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T06:18:04-07:00","id":1318663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1203449-request-editable-pdf-character-sheet?p=1318465#post1318465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there's some kind of eldritch chicanery at work here, Mr G. When the magic word 'sheets' is uttered aloud there's a clap of thunder, a little ozone frisson, and there you are, tipping your fedora with a knowing smile as you hand out PDF miracles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just have a knack for it I guess... lol<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1203449-request-editable-pdf-character-sheet?p=1318465#post1318465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My next character is gonna be a scion of you. Sure, he may not punch too many Jotnar to death with his fists but he'll damn well make them feel inadequate when he breaks out their character sheets and shows them how awful their stats are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha!! Thanks, I'd be honored. That sounds awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1203449-request-editable-pdf-character-sheet?p=1318471#post1318471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I bought the Origin PDF from DriveThru, it included both a non-interactive and an interactive character sheet in the download options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting.... they must have taken the one I sent and made a non-interactive version....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1203449-request-editable-pdf-character-sheet?p=1318506#post1318506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He has a special knack, he can spend a legend to materialise a high quality interactive sheet for any game, even those yet to be launched.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have my moments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And to note, I've had a sheet done for this for quite a long time now. Glad to finally be able to release it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T14:34:16-07:00","id":1319125,"title":"","content":"So while I can't, actually, play a Scion of Mr Gone, here's how I think it might go if I did:<br /> <br /> Things were bad. Things were really, really, bad. Atticus Shaw, chosen of Athena, stood wheezing back to back with his bandmate, Julian Fowler, chosen of Artemis. He was pretty certain, by the stabbing pain in his right side that two of his ribs were broken. Julian wasn\u2019t a whole lot better. The massive Cyclops that they\u2019d foolishly attacked in its own lair had been a much tougher opponent than they\u2019d expected.<br /> <br /> Atthicus paused and spat. Yes. There was blood in his saliva. Something inside him had ruptured, then. Wonderful. Idly he wondered if dying now would be a better fate than he would receive at Athena\u2019s hands when she came to rake him across the coals for his poor wisdom and battle strategy today.<br /> <br /> Ahead the Cyclops, easily twelve feet tall, grinned wickedly. He knew that he had the upper hand in this confrontation. With only a few nicks and scratches on its bronze coloured skin it was barely irritated much less seriously wounded. Cocky now, the giant hefted the steel girder that it had been using to slowly beat the two Scions to death and swished it back and forth. He was in no hurry. He knew how this was going to end.<br /> <br /> Or at least he thought he did.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t like your chances.\u201d<br /> <br /> A new voice, an unexpected one. All eyes turned to see the approaching figure, dressed like some kind of a pulp hero. His trenchcoat flared slightly in the wind, and the fedora perched atop his head was at the perfect angle, the front brim pulled down a little to cast the stranger\u2019s face in mysterious shadow.<br /> <br /> The Cyclops paused for a moment, then broke into a wicked grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m killing two of you.\u201d he announced with rumbling menace, \u201cI don\u2019t mind killing three.\u201d<br /> <br /> The figure shook his head slowly, in the manner of a parent expressing disappointment in an unruly child.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot with those stats.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Cyclops paused mid \u2018rumbling menace\u2019 and went from savage to confused.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> The figure reached under his trenchcoat and took out, of all things, a piece of paper with text printed on it. He pointed the paper in the direction of the Cyclops.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook at the attributes you\u2019ve got.\u201d he explained patiently, \u201cI mean you\u2019re clearly Nemesis level, there isn\u2019t any doubt about that, but look what they\u2019ve given you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Curious, the Cyclops lumbered over as Atticus and Julian watched on, trying to figure what the Hell was happening.<br /> <br /> The Cyclops peered at the displayed sheet and the newcomer jabbed a gloved finger at some of the text.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook. Your primary pool . . . I mean it\u2019s not <i>bad</i>, not really, but look what you\u2019ve got. Apocalyptic Presence? They\u2019re Scions. They\u2019re not going to be scared of that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey!\u201d replied the Cyclops, pouting a little. \u201cI\u2019m terrifying!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d allowed the stranger, \u201cTo mortals and puppies.\u201d<br /> <br /> He then pointed at the sheet again.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook at how you\u2019ve been statted up. Sure, you can smash things, but that doesn\u2019t leave you with a whole lot else does it? Collateral Damage? Really? So you can smash up your own lair. What\u2019s with that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI did wonder about that.\u201d admitted the Cyclops, rubbing at his bald head.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd a girder? Really? That\u2019s what you call a Mystic Arsenal?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh come on, man. That\u2019s just hurtful.\u201d<br /> <br /> The stranger shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re Scions. In a few minutes they\u2019re going to figure out that just hurling themselves at you won\u2019t work and they\u2019re going to get creative. You know how <i>that</i> works.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Cyclops scowled indignantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI hate it when that happens.\u201d<br /> <br /> The stranger nodded and pointed at the sheet again.<br /> <br /> \u201cFive Defense; it\u2019s not bad but you know that they\u2019re going to chip away at it. Then what have you got?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey!\u201d muttered the Cyclops, stung at the constant belittling. \u201cI\u2019ve got Second Wind! I\u2019m fine!\u201d<br /> <br /> The stranger peered up at the Cyclops. The shadows remained hiding his face, despite the direction of the lighting. And, despite his face being unseen, the figure still managed to convey a sceptical look at the massive Cyclops. <i>Cool trick</i>, thought Atticus.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re fine.\u201d repeated the stranger in a dry tone. \u201cYou\u2019re going to stake your life on \u2018I\u2019m fine because I have Second Wind\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Cyclops paused, took a moment to eye the two Scions, then sighed and hung his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo-ooo.\u201d he murmured, like a scolded child.<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t think so.\u201d replied the stranger.<br /> <br /> The Cyclops paused, then peered at the stranger.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m gonna go. Are you OK with these two morons?\u201d<br /> <br /> The stranger nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cI got it. You do what you have to do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cScrew this.\u201d muttered the Cyclops, \u201cI\u2019m heading back to the workshop and I\u2019m <i>not</i> coming back until I get some better Qualities and Flairs.\u201d<br /> <br /> The massive creatture lumbered out and Atticus stared, jaw slack, watching the figure go. And then, in reverential awe, he looked at the stranger.<br /> <br /> \u201cWho <i>are</i> you?\u201d<br /> <br /> The figure looked over and tipped the front of his fedora in a polite greeting.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe you want to worry less about your Warrior Knacks.\u201dhe added, \u201cFocus some more on your Sage Knacks. Maybe consider letting your Lover Calling go and looking at Creator. That spear of yours could use a few more tags.\u201d<br /> <br /> And then, as mysterioiusly as he came, the figure departed and was gone, and on the winds came the faint sound of his voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m Lore, by the way. Scion of Mr Gone.\u201d<br /> <br /> And then he was, like his patron, indeed gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Tah dah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.c